    symptoms: "Signs can include marked changes in eating patterns, skipping meals or eating in secret, rigid rules around food, frequent trips to the bathroom after eating, preoccupation with weight or body shape, significant weight change in either direction, excessive exercise, wearing baggy clothes to hide weight loss, and irritability or withdrawal around mealtimes. Physical signs such as fatigue, dizziness, hair thinning or menstrual changes can also point to an eating disorder, especially when they occur alongside changes in eating behaviour.",
