    symptoms: "In new fathers, this can look less like classic sadness and more like irritability, anger, withdrawal from the family, increased working hours as an avoidance strategy, fatigue, difficulty bonding with the baby, anxiety about providing financially, and, in some cases, increased alcohol use. Because these symptoms differ from the more commonly recognised presentation in mothers, they are easily mistaken for stress, tiredness or simply adjusting to a new routine rather than depression.",
