      "Signs that go beyond normal ageing include repeatedly asking the same question, getting lost in a previously familiar area, increasing difficulty managing money or medicines correctly, word-finding difficulty that noticeably disrupts conversation, withdrawing from usual activities or hobbies, and personality or judgment changes noticed by people close to the person. In contrast, normal ageing involves occasional forgetfulness — misplacing keys, briefly forgetting a name — without it affecting the person's ability to manage their usual responsibilities.",
